WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.125
An AI identity nobody watches
drifts the day after it's issued,

2
00:00:04.125 --> 00:00:07.162
and AI nobody declared
is drift from the start.

3
00:00:07.162 --> 00:00:10.689
So the program compares three
things: what was declared,

4
00:00:10.689 --> 00:00:14.675
what known identities are seen
doing, and what discovery finds.

5
00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:18.856
Shadow AI shows up in four
places: AI services staff use,

6
00:00:18.856 --> 00:00:25.175
apps holding consented access, agents on
endpoints, and AI built in your own clouds.

7
00:00:25.175 --> 00:00:29.125
No single tool sees all four,
and none sees a static key.

8
00:00:29.125 --> 00:00:32.268
Each gap becomes a finding
with an owner and a clock,

9
00:00:32.268 --> 00:00:34.588
and the serious ones halt for a person.

10
00:00:34.588 --> 00:00:37.424
Security operations contains shadow AI.

11
00:00:37.424 --> 00:00:43.162
Then the system owner decides its future,
or the CIO, when it belongs to no system.

12
00:00:43.162 --> 00:00:44.350
So who owns it?
